{"id": "silicon-valley-bart-extension-cost-and-oversight", "title": "The South Bay BART extension’s cost forecast rose as its opening moved to 2039", "seconds": 56.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.033, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "7b3a468068f893dd", "words": 153, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The Valley Transportation Authority leads construction. BART will operate the extension.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.73, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["When", "will", "the", "extension", "open?"], "sub": "Silicon Valley Phase II"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 1.03, 1.47, 1.71, 3.01, 3.3, 3.5, 3.84, 3.95]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "In 2021 federal reviewers forecast 9.148 billion dollars and a 2034 opening.", "t0": 4.85, "t1": 11.71, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "monitor", "kicker": "Federal Transit Administration, project management oversight contractor", "text": "October 2021", "mark": "October 2021"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.5, 1.09, 1.45, 1.89, 2.54, 2.85, 3.15, 3.44, 3.71, 3.94, 4.3, 4.87, 5.16, 5.24, 5.57, 6.13]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The cost and opening forecasts changed as design and risk estimates evolved.", "t0": 11.83, "t1": 15.96, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Capital cost estimates", "heading": "Three later forecasts", "source": "monitor", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "September 2022", "value": "$9.318 billion"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "October 2023", "value": "$12.237 billion"}, {"icon": "audit", "label": "March 2024", "value": "$12.746 billion"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.48, 0.61, 0.94, 1.5, 2.01, 2.2, 2.59, 2.69, 2.96, 3.4]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The March 2024 forecast included over three billion dollars in contingency.", "t0": 16.08, "t1": 20.23, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Contingency"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.37, 0.65, 1.13, 1.67, 2.1, 2.34, 2.63, 2.99, 3.3, 3.41]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The federal monitor still showed February 2039 as the approved opening baseline.", "t0": 20.35, "t1": 25.44, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "monitor", "kicker": "Federal Transit Administration, project management oversight contractor", "text": "October 2026 monitoring report", "mark": "October 2026 monitoring report"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.48, 0.9, 1.17, 1.47, 1.92, 2.22, 3.32, 3.56, 3.68, 4.16, 4.52]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Eligible spending through June 2026 was 16.2 percent of the budget.", "t0": 25.56, "t1": 30.22, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "16.2%", "label": "Eligible spending through June 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.47, 0.99, 1.27, 1.52, 1.78, 2.37, 2.59, 3.13, 3.39, 3.61, 3.99, 4.09, 4.2]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "BART's Inspector General found gaps in public communication about the tunnel design.", "t0": 30.44, "t1": 34.18, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "oig", "kicker": "BART independent Office of the Inspector General", "text": "BART Inspector General", "mark": "BART Inspector General"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.78, 1.11, 1.37, 1.72, 1.84, 2.15, 2.71, 2.89, 2.99, 3.28]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "BART accepted the modified design after its original safety concerns were addressed.", "t0": 34.3, "t1": 38.54, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Modified design"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.74, 0.87, 1.32, 1.75, 2.05, 2.22, 2.67, 3.02, 3.44, 3.58]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "The county grand jury questioned the funding strategy.", "t0": 38.66, "t1": 41.03, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "jury", "kicker": "Santa Clara County Civil Grand Jury", "text": "Civil grand jury finding", "mark": "Civil grand jury finding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.46, 0.72, 0.99, 1.36, 1.46, 1.79]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "VTA agreed it lacked an alternative strategy if planned funding failed.", "t0": 41.15, "t1": 45.46, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "response", "kicker": "Santa Clara Valley Transportation Authority", "text": "September 2026 response", "mark": "September 2026 response"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.95, 1.06, 1.33, 1.47, 2.05, 2.94, 3.17, 3.49, 3.91]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "It disputed a separate finding, saying it maintained a twenty-year cash flow model.", "t0": 45.58, "t1": 49.93, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Financial model"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.62, 0.71, 1.08, 1.79, 2.08, 2.18, 2.65, 2.73, 3.22, 3.48, 3.7]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The final cost and opening date remain unresolved.", "t0": 50.05, "t1": 52.86, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Final cost", "Opening date"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.47, 0.82, 0.95, 1.27, 1.49, 1.85]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 52.98, "t1": 55.28, "shot": "r12", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.7, 0.91, 1.23, 1.34, 1.44, 1.7, 1.95]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Four estimates", "review": "Design and funding oversight"}, "look": "map", "hook": "timeline"}